    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.20837v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        &hellip;(CIR) in big data environments. By using concepts such as cognitive similarity distances, metric spaces, retrieval topologies, etc., this paper aims to propose the semantic <span class="search-hit mathjax">alignment</span> between user queries and document repositories. The paper also extends this approach to incorporate logical connectives in cognitive information retrieval.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.20837v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2510.20837v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.20837v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Due to the exponential growth of big data in this digital era, an advanced method for effective information retrieval becomes essential. The basic objective of this paper is to propose a topology-based method for cognitive information retrieval (CIR) in big data environments. By using concepts such as cognitive similarity distances, metric spaces, retrieval topologies, etc., this paper aims to propose the semantic <span class="search-hit mathjax">alignment</span> between user queries and document repositories. The paper also extends this approach to incorporate logical connectives in cognitive information retrieval.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.20837v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2510.20837v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

