    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        InsideOut: Integrated RGB-Radiative Gaussian Splatting for Comprehensive 3D Object Representation
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Lee%2C+J">Jungmin Lee</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Hong%2C+S">Seonghyuk Hong</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Lee%2C+J">Juyong Lee</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Lee%2C+J">Jaeyoon Lee</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Choi%2C+J">Jongwon Choi</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.17864v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        &hellip;is invaluable in fields such as medical diagnostics, cultural heritage restoration, and manufacturing. We collect new paired RGB and X-ray data, perform hierarchical fitting to <span class="search-hit mathjax">align</span> RGB and X-ray radiative Gaussian splats, and propose an X-ray reference loss to ensure consistent internal structures. InsideOut effectively addresses the challenges posed by di&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.17864v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2510.17864v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.17864v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        We introduce InsideOut, an extension of 3D Gaussian splatting (3DGS) that bridges the gap between high-fidelity RGB surface details and subsurface X-ray structures. The fusion of RGB and X-ray imaging is invaluable in fields such as medical diagnostics, cultural heritage restoration, and manufacturing. We collect new paired RGB and X-ray data, perform hierarchical fitting to <span class="search-hit mathjax">align</span> RGB and X-ray radiative Gaussian splats, and propose an X-ray reference loss to ensure consistent internal structures. InsideOut effectively addresses the challenges posed by disparate data representations between the two modalities and limited paired datasets. This approach significantly extends the applicability of 3DGS, enhancing visualization, simulation, and non-destructive testing capabilities across various domains.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.17864v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2510.17864v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 15 October, 2025; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> October 2025.
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="comments is-size-7">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Comments:</span>
      <span class="has-text-grey-dark mathjax">Published at ICCV 2025</span>
    </p>
    

    

    
